Recommends: homelab-dns, homelab-postfix, homelab-api
Description: DNS + mail-domain administration for the homelab-* ecosystem
 Owns "what domains are we authoritative for, and what is their DKIM/
 mail-routing state" as one cohesive concern, fronted by homelab-api's
 /api/v1/domains/* gateway route (see ../api/README.md) the same way
 homelab-mailbridge backs /api/v1/mail/*. Talks to PowerDNS via its own
 built-in HTTP API (not a direct grant on PowerDNS's separate database,
 not pdnsutil) for zone/record CRUD, and keeps homelab-postfix's notion
 of valid mail domains in sync via a shared `domainadmin` schema in the
 one shared `homelab` database (split runtime/migrate roles, see
 CLAUDE.md). A later release adds DKIM key generation/rotation
 (deliberately never storing private key material in Postgres -- see
 README.md) and per-recipient mail allow/block. Must be installed on
 the SAME host as homelab-postfix/OpenDKIM -- see README.md's
 "Deployment topology" section.
